# Python docstrings

Use [Sphinx](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/usage/restructuredtext/domains.html#info-field-lists) docstrings (reStructuredText info field lists). English only.

- First line: one sentence, what the class or function does.
- Blank line, then one `:param name:` field per argument.
- Align the descriptions with spaces so they start in the same column.
- A returned value gets `:return:`. Use `:rtype:` only when the type is not already in the signature.
- An exception the caller must handle gets `:raises ExceptionType:`.
- A function with no arguments, return value, or raised exceptions is the summary sentence only.

```python
def load(self, filename: str, inform):
    """
    Loads the defaults from a file on disk, performing migration if required.

    :param filename:    a path to the file that is to be loaded
    :param inform:      a pyqtSignal used to display information in the status bar

    :return:            True when the file was loaded

    :raises OSError:    the file could not be read
    :raises ValueError: the file contents are not valid defaults
    """
```

Do not use Google style (`Args:`) or NumPy style (`Parameters`).
